This product includes PortSimEnv v1 by Adithya S Kolavi, part of FineEnvs
(https://github.com/adithya-s-k/FineEnvs, 07-simulation-environments/portsim-v1, commit b0f4c2f),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Derived from it:

- berth_core (envs/berth_planning/core/): not copied; the package depends on it at that commit and the
  env image installs it from there.
- src/agentenv_portsim/server.py: the MCP tools get_situation, check_plan and submit_plan (names,
  descriptions, input schemas, output and error text, limits) are ported from
  envs/berth_planning/openenv/berth_openenv/environment.py.
- agents/portsim-llm/agent.py: the harness loop (turns, nudges, notes, limits, the episode record) and
  its Anthropic Messages, OpenAI Responses and chat-completions adapters are ported from
  envs/berth_planning/openenv/berth_openenv/agent.py.
- src/agentenv_portsim/tasks.py: the opening message is copied from
  envs/berth_planning/openenv/berth_openenv/agent.py; src/agentenv_portsim/sweep.py: ci() is copied
  from eval/report.py.
- src/agentenv_portsim/world.py: naive() adapts naive_replan's greedy search from
  envs/berth_planning/core/berth_core/solve.py to keep frozen windows and start the rest at or after
  the freeze line.
- scripts/live_references.py: the CP-SAT model in solve() is adapted from optimal_plan in
  envs/berth_planning/core/berth_core/solve.py, with frozen windows pinned and the rest held at or
  after the freeze line.
- scripts/marine_references.py: solves with scripts/live_references.py's solve(), adapted from
  optimal_plan as above, adding a cumulative constraint for the port's pilots and one for its tugs.
- scripts/wind_references.py: solves with scripts/live_references.py's solve(), adapted from
  optimal_plan as above, and scripts/marine_references.py's pilot and tug constraints.
- src/agentenv_portsim/web/upstream/: PortSimEnv's viewer, copied unchanged from
  envs/berth_planning/openenv/berth_openenv/web/.
- src/agentenv_portsim/web/ext/index.html: adapted from that viewer's index.html (its import map,
  title and header).
- src/agentenv_portsim/web/ext/overview.js: adapted from that viewer's overview.js (the leaderboard and
  the episode table).
- src/agentenv_portsim/web/ext/live.js: the transcript loop is adapted from that viewer's transcript.js.
- src/agentenv_portsim/view.py: the /api routes and their JSON follow
  envs/berth_planning/openenv/berth_openenv/api.py; src/agentenv_portsim/episodes.py: the episode
  summaries follow summarize() in eval/run_eval.py.

Data licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (data/LICENSE), not under the Apache License:

- data/dock-v1-eval/ and data/dock-v1-train/: PortSimEnv's dock-v1 task packs, copied unchanged from
  envs/berth_planning/tasks/.
- tests/golden/: outputs recorded from PortSimEnv on dock-v1 tasks.
- The plans in src/agentenv_portsim/bundles/portsim/tasks/, taken from the dock-v1 task packs.
- data/live/references.jsonl: rolling and naive reference plans and costs computed from the dock-v1
  task packs.
- src/agentenv_portsim/bundles/portsim-live/tasks/: prompts and notices taken from the dock-v1 task
  packs.
- data/dock-v1-marine/: the one-week weeks of the dock-v1-eval pack with the port's pilots and tugs;
  the other traffic in each week's rules is derived from the Port of Barcelona's 2024 calls of every
  ship type, generator/raw/Barcelona_2024.csv in
  https://github.com/alberto-santini/berth-allocation-problems at commit 8e726a4, licensed under
  CC BY-SA 4.0 and not included here; manifest.json records its sha256, how it was derived and the
  public sources of the pools and rules.
- data/marine/references.jsonl: rolling and naive reference plans and costs computed from
  data/dock-v1-marine/.
- src/agentenv_portsim/bundles/portsim-marine/tasks/: prompts and notices taken from
  data/dock-v1-marine/.
- data/dock-v1-wind/: weeks of data/dock-v1-marine/ moved into the weather weeks of
  data/wind/weather.jsonl; manifest.json records how, with the public sources of the wind rules and the
  pins of the weather's sources. The weather in it keeps its sources' terms (below).
- data/wind/references.jsonl: hindsight, rolling, blind, hold and naive reference plans and costs
  computed from data/dock-v1-wind/.
- src/agentenv_portsim/bundles/portsim-wind/tasks/: prompts and notices taken from data/dock-v1-wind/;
  the forecast notices keep their sources' terms (below).
- tests/wind/fixtures/: weeks of data/dock-v1-marine/ in synthetic weather; no reading or forecast in
  them is real.
- data/published/dock-eval50/index.json: the published dock-eval50 results, copied unchanged from
  results/rollouts/dock-eval50/index.json.
- tests/viewer/runs/: episodes recorded on dock-v1 tasks; their transcripts hold the task text.
- tests/viewer/marine_runs/: a week played on data/dock-v1-marine/ by two scripted policies; their
  transcripts hold the task text.
- tests/viewer/wind_runs/: a week played on tests/wind/fixtures/ by two scripted policies; their
  transcripts hold the task text.
- assets/live-week.gif: a recorded live week on the viewer; it also shows the 3D twin (below).

The viewer's 3D twin of the Port of Barcelona is not included: agent-env portsim view and record
download it from PortSimEnv's public bucket. It is © OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the
Open Database License 1.0 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright), with terrain from Terrain Tiles on
AWS (twin/SOURCES.md). Images and videos rendered from it carry the attribution "© OpenStreetMap
